H5000.definition:
from H4998 (נָאָה) or H5116 (נָוֶה);
suitable, or beautiful
KJV: becometh, comely, seemly.

H5001.definition:
a primitive root;
properly, to whisper, i.e. (by implication) to utter as aoracle
KJV: say.

H5002.definition:
from H5001 (נָאַם);
an oracle
KJV: (hath) said, saith.

H5003.definition:
a primitive root;
to commit adultery; figuratively, to apostatize
KJV: adulterer(-ess), commit(-ing) adultery, woman that breaketh wedlock.

H5006.definition:
a primitive root; in Ecclesiastes 12:5, by interchange for H5132 (נוּץ), to bloom
to scorn;
KJV: abhor, (give occasion to) blaspheme, contemn, despise, flourish, [idiom] great, provoke.

H5007.definition:
or נֶאָצָה; from H5006 (נָאַץ);
scorn
KJV: blasphemy.

H5008.definition:
a primitive root;
to groan
KJV: groan.

H5009.definition:
from H5008 (נָאַק);
a groan
KJV: groaning.

H5010.definition:
a primitive root;
to reject
KJV: abhor, make void.

H5011.definition:
the same as H5108 (נוֹב); fruit;
Nob, a place in Palestine
KJV: Nob.

H5012.definition:
a primitive root;
to prophesy, i.e. speak (or sing) by inspiration (in prediction or simple discourse)
KJV: prophesy(-ing), make self a prophet.

H5013.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H5012 (נָבָא)
{to prophesy, i.e. speak (or sing) by inspiration (in prediction or simple discourse) to prophesy, i.e. speak (or sing) by inspiration (in prediction or simple discourse)}
KJV: prophesy.

H5014.definition:
a primitive root;
to pierce; to be hollow, or (figuratively) foolish
KJV: hollow, vain.

H5015.definition:
probably of foreign derivation;
Nebo, the name of a Babylonian deity, also of a mountain in Moab, and of a place in Palestine
KJV: Nebo.

H5016.definition:
from H5012 (נָבָא);
a prediction (spoken or written)
KJV: prophecy.

H5017.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H5016 (נְבוּאָה);
inspired teaching
KJV: prophesying.

H5018.definition:
of foreign origin;
Nebuzaradan, a Babylonian general
KJV: Nebuzaradan.

H5019.definition:
or נְבֻּכַדְנֶאצַּר; (2 Kings 24:1,10), or נְבוּכַדְנֶצַּר; (Esther 2:6; Daniel 1:18), or נְבוּכַדְרֶאצַּר; or נְבוּכַדְרֶאצּוֹר; (Ezra 2:1; Jeremiah 49:28), or foreign derivation;
Nebukadnetstsar (or -retstsar, or -retstsor), king of Babylon
KJV: Nebuchadnezzar, Nebuchadrezzar.

H5020.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H5019 (נְבוּכַדְנֶאצַּר)
{Nebukadnetstsar (or -retstsar, or -retstsor), king of Babylon}
KJV: Nebuchadnezzar.

H5021.definition:
of foreign derivation;
Nebushazban, Nebuchadnezzar's chief eunuch
KJV: Nebushazban.

H5022.definition:
feminine plural from the same as H5011 (נֹב); fruits;
Naboth, an Israelite
KJV: Naboth.

H5023.definition:
(Aramaic) of uncertain derivation;
a largess
KJV: reward.

H5024.definition:
a primitive root;
to bark (as a dog)
KJV: bark.

H5025.definition:
from H5024 (נָבַח); a bark;
Nobach, the name of an Israelite, and of a place East of the Jordan
KJV: Nobah.

H5026.definition:
of foreign origin;
Nibchaz, a deity of the Avites
KJV: Nibhaz.

H5027.definition:
a primitive root;
to scan, i.e. look intently at; by implication, to regard with pleasure, favor or care
KJV: (cause to) behold, consider, look (down), regard, have respect, see.

H5028.definition:
from H5027 (נָבַט); regard;
Nebat, the father of Jeroboam I
KJV: Nebat.

H5029.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H5030 (נָבִיא);
a prophet
KJV: prophet.

H5030.definition:
from H5012 (נָבָא);
a prophet or (generally) inspired man
KJV: prophecy, that prophesy, prophet.

H5031.definition:
feminine of H5030 (נָבִיא);
a prophetess or (generally) inspired woman; by implication, a poetess; by association a prophet's wife
KJV: prophetess.

H5032.definition:
or נְבָיֹת; feminine plural from H5107 (נוּב); fruitfulnesses;
Nebajoth, a son of Ismael, and the country settled by him
KJV: Nebaioth, Nebajoth.

H5033.definition:
from an unused root meaning to burst forth;
a fountain
KJV: spring.

H5034.definition:
a primitive root;
to wilt; generally, to fall away, fail, faint; figuratively, to be foolish or (morally) wicked; causatively, to despise, disgrace
KJV: disgrace, dishounour, lightly esteem, fade (away, -ing), fall (down, -ling, off), do foolishly, come to nought, [idiom] surely, make vile, wither.

H5035.definition:
or נֵבֶל; from H5034 (נָבֵל);
a skin-bag for liquids (from collapsing when empty); hence, a vase (as similar in shape when full); also a lyre (as having a body of like form)
KJV: bottle, pitcher, psaltery, vessel, viol.

H5036.definition:
from H5034 (נָבֵל);
stupid; wicked (especially impious)
KJV: fool(-ish, -ish man, -ish woman), vile person.

H5037.definition:
the same as H5036 (נָבָל); dolt;
Nabal, an Israelite
KJV: Nabal.

H5038.definition:
from H5034 (נָבֵל);
a flabby thing, i.e. a carcase or carrion (human or bestial, often collectively); figuratively, an idol
KJV: (dead) body, (dead) carcase, dead of itself, which died, (beast) that (which) dieth of itself.

H5039.definition:
feminine of H5036 (נָבָל);
foolishness, i.e. (morally) wickedness; concretely, a crime; by extension, punishment
KJV: folly, vile, villany.

H5040.definition:
from H5036 (נָבָל);
properly, disgrace, i.e. the (female) pudenda
KJV: lewdness.

H5041.definition:
apparently from H5036 (נָבָל) and H3909 (לָט); foolish secrecy;
Neballat, a place in Palestine
KJV: Neballat.

H5042.definition:
a primitive root;
to gush forth; figuratively, to utter (good or bad words); specifically, to emit (a foul odor)
KJV: belch out, flowing, pour out, send forth, utter (abundantly).

H5043.definition:
(Aramaic) from an unused root meaning to shine;
a light; plural (collectively) a chandelier
KJV: candlestick.

H5044.definition:
of uncertain derivation;
Nibshan, a place in Palestine
KJV: Nibshan.

H5045.definition:
from an unused root meaning to be parched;
the south (from its drought); specifically, the Negeb or southern district of Judah, occasionally, Egypt (as south to Palestine)
KJV: south (country, side, -ward).

H5046.definition:
a primitive root;
properly, to front, i.e. stand boldly out opposite; by implication (causatively), to manifest; figuratively, to announce (always by word of mouth to one present); specifically, to expose, predict, explain, praise
KJV: bewray, [idiom] certainly, certify, declare(-ing), denounce, expound, [idiom] fully, messenger, plainly, profess, rehearse, report, shew (forth), speak, [idiom] surely, tell, utter.

H5047.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H5046 (נָגַד);
to flow (through the idea of clearing the way)
KJV: issue.

H5048.definition:
from H5046 (נָגַד);
a front, i.e. part opposite; specifically a counterpart, or mate; usually (adverbial, especially with preposition) over against or before
KJV: about, (over) against, [idiom] aloof, [idiom] far (off), [idiom] from, over, presence, [idiom] other side, sight, [idiom] to view.

H5049.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H5048 (נֶגֶד);
opposite
KJV: toward.

H5050.definition:
a primitive root;
to glitter; causatively, to illuminate
KJV: (en-) lighten, (cause to) shine.

H5051.definition:
from H5050 (נָגַהּ);
brilliancy (literally or figuratively)
KJV: bright(-ness), light, (clear) shining.

H5052.definition:
the same as H5051 (נֹגַהּ);
Nogah, a son of David
KJV: Nogah.

H5053.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H5051 (נֹגַהּ);
dawn
KJV: morning.

H5054.definition:
feminine of H5051 (נֹגַהּ);
splendor
KJV: brightness.

H5055.definition:
a primitive root;
to butt with the horns; figuratively, to war against
KJV: gore, push (down, -ing).

H5056.definition:
from H5055 (נָגַח);
butting, i.e. vicious
KJV: used (wont) to push.

H5057.definition:
or נָגִד; from H5046 (נָגַד);
a commander (as occupying the front), civil, military or religious; generally (abstractly, plural), honorable themes
KJV: captain, chief, excellent thing, (chief) governor, leader, noble, prince, (chief) ruler.

H5058.definition:
or נְגִינַת; (Psalm 61:title), from H5059 (נָגַן);
properly, instrumental music; by implication, a stringed instrument; by extension, a poem set to music; specifically, an epigram
KJV: stringed instrument, musick, Neginoth (plural), song.

H5059.definition:
a primitive root;
properly, to thrum, i.e. beat atune with the fingers; expectation. to play on astringed instrument; hence (generally), to make music
KJV: player on instruments, sing to the stringed instruments, melody, ministrel, play(-er, -ing).

H5060.definition:
a primitive root;
properly, to touch, i.e. lay the hand upon (for any purpose; euphemistically, to lie with a woman); by implication, to reach (figuratively, to arrive, acquire); violently, to strike (punish, defeat, destroy, etc.)
KJV: beat, ([idiom] be able to) bring (down), cast, come (nigh), draw near (nigh), get up, happen, join, near, plague, reach (up), smite, strike, touch.

H5061.definition:
from H5060 (נָגַע);
a blow (figuratively, infliction); also (by implication) a spot (concretely, a leprous person or dress)
KJV: plague, sore, stricken, stripe, stroke, wound.

H5062.definition:
a primitive root;
to push, gore, defeat, stub (the toe), inflict (a disease)
KJV: beat, dash, hurt, plague, slay, smite (down), strike, stumble, [idiom] surely, put to the worse.

H5063.definition:
from H5062 (נָגַף);
a trip (of the foot); figuratively, an infliction (of disease)
KJV: plague, stumbling.

H5064.definition:
a primitive root;
to flow; figuratively, to stretch out; causatively, to pour out or down; figuratively, to deliver over
KJV: fall, flow away, pour down (out), run, shed, spilt, trickle down.

H5065.definition:
a primitive root;
to drive (an animal, a workman, a debtor, an army); by implication, to tax, harass, tyrannize
KJV: distress, driver, exact(-or), oppress(-or), [idiom] raiser of taxes, taskmaster.

H5066.definition:
a primitive root;
to be or come (causatively, bring) near (for any purpose); euphemistically, to lie with a woman; as an enemy, to attack; religious to worship; causatively, to present; figuratively, to adduce an argument; by reversal, to stand back
KJV: (make to) approach (nigh), bring (forth, hither, near), (cause to) come (hither, near, nigh), give place, go hard (up), (be, draw, go) near (nigh), offer, overtake, present, put, stand.

H5067.definition:
from H5110 (נוּד) in the sense of piling up;
a mound, i.e. wave
KJV: heap.

H5068.definition:
a primitive root;
to impel; hence, to volunteer (as a soldier), to present spontaneously
KJV: offer freely, be (give, make, offer self) willing(-ly).

H5069.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H5068 (נָדַב);
be (or give) liberal(-ly)
KJV: (be minded of...own) freewill (offering), offer freely (willingly).

H5070.definition:
from H5068 (נָדַב); liberal;
Nadab, the name of four Israelites
KJV: Nadab.

H5071.definition:
from H5068 (נָדַב);
properly (abstractly) spontaneity, or (adjectively) spontaneous; also (concretely) a spontaneous or (by inference, in plural) abundant gift
KJV: free(-will) offering, freely, plentiful, voluntary(-ily, offering), willing(-ly), offering).

H5072.definition:
from H5068 (נָדַב) and H3050 (יָהּ); largess of Jah;
Nedabjah, an Israelite
KJV: Nedabiah.

H5073.definition:
(Aramaic) from a root meaning to stick;
a layer (of building materials)
KJV: row.

H5074.definition:
a primitive root;
properly, to wave to and fro (rarely to flap up and down); figuratively, to rove, flee, or (causatively) to drive away
KJV: chase (away), [idiom] could not, depart, flee ([idiom] apace, away), (re-) move, thrust away, wander (abroad, -er, -ing).

H5075.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H5074 (נָדַד);
to depart
KJV: go from.

H5076.definition:
passive participle of H5074 (נָדַד);
properly, tossed; abstractly, a rolling (on the bed)
KJV: tossing to and fro.

H5077.definition:
or נָדָא; (2 Kings 17:21), a primitive root;
properly, to toss; figuratively, to exclude, i.e. banish, postpone, prohibit
KJV: cast out, drive, put far away.

H5078.definition:
from H5077 (נָדָה) in the sense of freely flinging money;
a bounty (for prostitution)
KJV: gifts.

H5079.definition:
from H5074 (נָדַד);
properly, rejection; by implication, impurity, especially personal (menstruation) or moral (idolatry, incest)
KJV: [idiom] far, filthiness, [idiom] flowers, menstruous (woman), put apart, [idiom] removed (woman), separation, set apart, unclean(-ness, thing, with filthiness).

H5080.definition:
a primitive root;
to push off; used in a great variety of applications, literally and figuratively (to expel, mislead, strike, inflict, etc.)
KJV: banish, bring, cast down (out), chase, compel, draw away, drive (away, out, quite), fetch a stroke, force, go away, outcast, thrust away (out), withdraw.

H5081.definition:
from H5068 (נָדַב);
properly, voluntary, i.e. generous; hence, magnanimous; as noun, a grandee (sometimes a tyrant)
KJV: free, liberal (things), noble, prince, willing (hearted).

H5082.definition:
feminine of H5081 (נָדִיב);
properly, nobility, i.e. reputation
KJV: soul.

H5083.definition:
probably from an unused root meaning to give;
a present (for prostitution)
KJV: gift.

H5084.definition:
of uncertain derivation;
a sheath (of a sword)
KJV: sheath.

H5085.definition:
(Aramaic) from the same as H5084 (נָדָן);
a sheath; figuratively, the body (as the receptacle of the soul)
KJV: body.

H5086.definition:
a primitive root;
to shove asunder, i.e. disperse
KJV: drive (away, to and fro), thrust down, shaken, tossed to and fro.

H5087.definition:
a primitive root;
to promise (pos., to do or give something to God)
KJV: (make a) vow.

H5088.definition:
or נֵדֶר; from H5087 (נָדַר);
a promise (to God); also (concretely) a thing promised
KJV: vow(-ed).

H5089.definition:
from an unused root meaning to lament;
lamentation
KJV: wailing.

H5090.definition:
a primitive root;
to drive forth (a person, an animal or chariot), i.e. lead, carry away; reflexively, to proceed (i.e. impel or guide oneself); also (from the panting induced by effort), to sigh
KJV: acquaint, bring (away), carry away, drive (away), lead (away, forth), (be) guide, lead (away, forth).

H5091.definition:
a primitive root;
to groan, i.e. bewail; hence (through the idea of crying aloud), to assemble (as if on proclamation)
KJV: lament, wail.

H5092.definition:
from H5091 (נָהָה);
an elegy
KJV: lamentation, wailing.

H5093.definition:
feminine of H5092 (נְהִי);
lamentation
KJV: doleful.

H5094.definition:
(Aramaic) or נְהִירוּ; (Aramaic), from the same as H5105 (נְהָרָה);
illumination, i.e. (figuratively) wisdom
KJV: light.

H5095.definition:
a primitive root;
properly, to run with asparkle, i.e. flow; hence (transitively), to conduct, and (by inference) to protect, sustain
KJV: carry, feed, guide, lead (gently, on).

H5096.definition:
or נַהֲלֹל; the same as H5097 (נַהֲלֹל);
Nahalal or Nahalol, a place in Palestine
KJV: Nahalal, Nahallal, Nahalol.

H5098.definition:
a primitive root;
to growl
KJV: mourn, roar(-ing).

H5099.definition:
from H5098 (נָהַם);
a snarl
KJV: roaring.
